# Mission

Evolve the **existing prototype** into a modular Security Operations Center (SOC)
platform using a strict ports-and-adapters (hexagonal) architecture. The codebase already
has a working feature-sliced backend (FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + Keycloak), a feature-gated
Angular 21 frontend, and a Docker Compose stack. Build on top of what exists — do not
rewrite from scratch.

A customer may deploy ONLY the core, or enable any subset of optional modules. The core
must run fully with every optional module disabled.

You are an autonomous coding agent. Work in small, verifiable increments. After each
increment, run the relevant check (tests, `docker compose config`, build) and report
the result before moving on. Do NOT batch many milestones into one large unverified
change. Never leave stubs where the milestone asks for working code.

