# Non-negotiable architectural invariants

1. Slice by business capability, never by third-party product.
2. The core (alerts, incidents, rules, admin/RBAC, audit, module_registry, outbox/event
   bus) must run without any optional module, provider, or external service.
3. Optional modules are independently enableable/disableable via config + Compose profile.
4. Disabled modules FAIL CLOSED via null/no-op adapters and hidden frontend routes — never
   via runtime errors. The existing feature-guard middleware in `main.py` already blocks
   disabled routes with 403 — enhance it to return the standard disabled-response shape
   instead of a generic 403.
5. Angular must NEVER call MISP, IRIS, n8n, AI, OpenSearch, or fleet providers directly.
6. Backend domain code must NEVER import vendor clients or external API schemas.
7. Vendor-specific payloads live ONLY in adapters, fixtures, and adapter audit records.
8. All external systems are reached through internal ports (interfaces).
9. Every adapter has contract tests (real + null variants).
10. Every state-changing action is audit logged.
11. Every external adapter call records: adapter name, adapter version, port, operation,
    status, latency_ms, request/response payload hash, external correlation id (if any),
    error_type. No secrets in audit records.
12. Frontend navigation/routes are generated from backend module enablement + RBAC
    permissions — not from build-time feature flags. The existing `FeatureService` in
    `core/services/feature.service.ts` must be refactored to call `/api/me/modules`
    instead of reading `runtimeConfig.features`. The hardcoded `navigationItems` array
    in `app.component.ts` must be replaced with backend-driven config.

