# Required internal ports (define BEFORE any vendor client)

These are Python ABCs in `backend/src/ports/`. The existing codebase has no port layer —
create it.

`LogCollectorRulePort`, `FleetLocationProviderPort`, `MapProviderPort`,
`CaseManagementPort`, `ThreatIntelPort`, `EventSearchPort`, `WorkflowPort`,
`AIEnrichmentPort`, and `IdentityProviderPort` if needed (Keycloak auth is already
handled by `core/auth.py` — only add this port if there's a second identity source).

Provide a Null adapter for every optional port (e.g. `NullThreatIntelAdapter`,
`NullCaseManagementAdapter`, `NullWorkflowAdapter`, `NullAIAdapter`,
`NullFleetProviderAdapter`, `NullMapProviderAdapter`, `NullEventSearchAdapter`).
Null adapters return controlled responses and never raise on the normal disabled path:

```json
{ "enabled": false, "reason": "module_not_enabled" }
```

