# Module registry contract

The existing `core/router.py` exposes `/api/v1/core/features` as a simple list. Replace
this with `/api/me/modules` and `/api/admin/modules` that expose canonical module ids
and enough metadata to drive routing and disabled-state handling. Minimum record shape:

```json
{
  "id": "threat_intel",
  "enabled": false,
  "status": "disabled",
  "reason": "module_not_enabled",
  "routes": ["/ti"],
  "required_permissions": ["threat_intel:read"],
  "dependencies": ["misp"],
  "provider": { "id": "null", "configured": false }
}
```

`status` is one of: `enabled`, `disabled`, `not_configured`, `degraded`.

The existing `FeatureRegistry` in `features/registry.py` and `FeatureState` in
`core/database.py` should be extended (not replaced) to produce this shape.

